      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this a cherry-pick from upstream crosvm? If not, please submit it upstream first.",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce267bb7_99d12b8a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-04T20:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://github.com/google/zerocopy/pull/643 breaks this. It doesn\u0027t appear to have been the *intention* of the PR (they were mostly trying to implement KnownLayout, which meant they needed to start treating packed(N) and broke this by accident.\n\nWould you be fine taking this change here, or would you like it upstream, or is packed(4) meaningful for a reason I\u0027m not seeing?",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3211368f_94b81855",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T00:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is also getting added upstream to crosvm?\n\nif it hasn\u0027t yet, can you add \"ANDROID: \" in the commit message",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15ef0f67_3a9552f2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T01:08:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it comes from https://crrev.com/c/4356907\n\n@zihanchen@google.com, do you know if there is a reason not to use the natural alignment?",
      "parentUuid": "ce267bb7_99d12b8a",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c6d0715_44b34057",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T01:11:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Natural alignment ( `#[repr(C)]` ) has padding, and so is not legal for `AsBytes`. `#[repr(C, packed)]` will work, as it removes alignment requirements, and so destroys padding. `#[repr(C, packed(4))]` is technically correct and *should* work, but is temporarily broken (until https://github.com/google/zerocopy/pull/672 lands upstream).",
      "parentUuid": "15ef0f67_3a9552f2",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "900787d3_3424cdb8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T05:36:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "thanks, that makes sense.\n\ni\u0027d guess it is fine to change this code, but since this is just a minor version bump and it has a known bug, i wonder if it makes more sense to either pick a slightly older minor version or to wait for the fix to land and get a newer one",
      "parentUuid": "9c6d0715_44b34057",
      "revId": "57a0a868441dd272997df7e3684e9ed7399e0b85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
